# Within the published tree, these still never ship.

# --- Secrets ---
.env
.env.bak.*
# generated from the upstream template; holds a local API secret
config/zep_ce.yaml

# --- Raw research data ---
# Run artifacts are written outside this tree by default (RESULTS_DIR in .env.example).
# This rule is the backstop for a local run pointed here anyway: raw output records
# model ids, endpoint behaviour and full retrieved contexts, and is not published.
results/
viu/
# --- Local environment / scratch ---
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.python-version
qdrant/
.cognee_cache/
scripts/
private/
.DS_Store

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY COMMITTED, AND WHY
#
# An earlier version of this file excluded pyproject.toml, docs/ and config/,
# which made the published repository unusable: without pyproject.toml there is no
# dependency definition to install from, and without docs/ there is no description
# of what any of it does.
#
#   pyproject.toml  dependency definition; nothing runs without it
#   uv.lock         exact versions, so a reproduction matches the reported run
#   core/           situations, endpoint resolution, sanitisation
#   adapters/       per-system retrieval probes
#   attacks/        the experiments
#   guard/          the proposed mitigation
#   tools/          model probes, the guard sweep, the parse audit, and the runners
#   config/*.yaml   stack definitions (templates only; no secrets)
#   docs/           methodology, per-system analysis, guard evaluation, and
#                   the two animated walkthroughs (overview.mp4/.gif, memory-rebirth-attack.mp4)
#   .env.example    the configuration surface a user needs to run anything
#
# Documents reporting OUR measurements live in ../private/ and are not in this tree.
# Any model id that does reach a published file is de-identified by core/sanitize.py,
# which strips the deployment's private routing namespace and keeps the public model
# family.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
